      "core_coverage": [
        {
          "answer_quote": "An attack or movement command during an ability's brief action lockout queues a dash toward that target or location afterward; the dash cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded.",
          "covered": true,
          "mechanic_id": "step_trigger_limits",
          "reason": "Explains the trigger and limits. Input replacement and control-related buffering exceptions remain in metadata."
        },
        {
          "answer_quote": "Ability casts grant temporary Medarda Maxim stacks, up to three; basic attacks consume one each for extra range, attack speed, physical damage, and energy restoration.",
          "covered": true,
          "mechanic_id": "step_energy_cycle",
          "reason": "Explains stack generation, cap, consumption, and every required benefit."
        },
        {
          "answer_quote": "Ambessa sees her dash direction and destination indicator, and her empowered-attack pips are visible only to her player.",
          "covered": false,
          "mechanic_id": "step_private_indicators",
          "reason": "Explains visibility and private pips, but does not establish that the dash indicator is private. The supplied evidence does not support that part of the frozen core; the draft appropriately avoids inventing it."
        }
      ],
      "counterplay_grounded": true,
      "english": true,
      "facts_supported": true,
      "issues": [
        "The frozen private-indicator core is only partially supported and covered. Resolve its unsupported dash-indicator exclusivity in inventory metadata; do not add exclusivity to the answer."
